      "Small victories hidden inside broken ideas\n\nMy hard drive holds more abandoned prototypes than finished games. At first that felt embarrassing. Now I see it as a record of fast, cheap learning. Each failure answered a question I could never have answered by thinking alone.\n\nLessons From the Graveyard\nFun comes first\nIf the core action is not satisfying within ten seconds, no amount of polish will rescue it.\nCut features early\nEvery extra system multiplies the bugs and hides the real idea.\n\nMy Prototype Checklist\nCan a stranger understand the goal without instructions?\nIs the main action fun on its own?\nHave I removed one feature this week?\nShare rough builds early. Players will find problems you have stopped noticing.\n\nFinal Thoughts\nA broken prototype is not a wasted weekend. It is a cheap lesson, and the next idea always starts a little smarter.\n\nGenerated by Claude\n",
